'''Master Uril''' (達人ウリル, ''Tatsujin Uriru'', '''Master Uril''') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy found on the [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|50th floor]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], which awards his [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Cat Unit counterpart]] via [[Catnip Challenges]] when completed. He was added in [[Version 9.6 Update|Version 9.6]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Master Uril
|image = E 516.png
|appearance = [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Heavenly Tower - Floor 50]]
|money drop = 2,222¢ - 8,777¢
}}

==Enemy==
Master Uril is one tough enemy to defeat. He isn't the fastest, but deals extremely high damage with a fast attack rate, as well as an Omni Strike outranging many units. Topping this off is his guaranteed level 3 [[Surge Attack|Surge]] and curse, meaning next to nothing will be able to withstand him for long.

Aside from using units with greater range and those that can get around his Surge (such as [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]), some options for stalling him include [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]], [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Heavy]]. These units work particularly well with their [[True Form]]s and, in Cyberpunk Cat's case, boosted Slow [[Talents]].

With [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]]'s Target Traitless and Immune to Surge Ultra [[Talents]], every single hit that Klay gets off will knockback Uril.

