==Trivia==
*The name Uril may be derived from [[wikipedia:Uriel|Uriel]], a figure in Jewish and Christian religions who is considered a master of knowledge and wisdom. Uriel is an archangel, which may relate to how [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] is said to have sealed away the demon king.
*He is a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:Dende|Dende]], a character from ''[[wikia:dragonball:Main Page|Dragon Ball]]''. In addition to Uril and Dende having similar designs, [[Heavenly Tower]] [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] resembles [[wikia:dragonball:The Lookout|Kami's Lookout]], which is overtaken by Dende.
**Master Uril's attack animation is also similar to the [[wikia:dragonball:Evil Containment Wave|Evil Containment Wave]], which was used against [[wikia:dragonball:King Piccolo|Great Demon King Piccolo]] like how Mystic Uril is said to have sealed away the demon king.
*Master Uril is implied to be related to [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] and [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]]; all three have white and spiky hair, wear tribal masks and joined the Cat Army on their own volition, and both Uril and Yulala reside in the [[Heavenly Tower]].
**Mystic Uril's description indicates that his grandchild gave him his mask. Since Ururun Wolf wears a similar-looking mask, Ururun is most likely Uril's granddaughter, and since Ururun is implied to be Yulala's daughter, Uril is most likely Yulala's father. Furthermore, Mystic Mask Yulala's Japanese description calls him the head of his clan, and enemy Master Uril's Japanese description says he passed down that same title to his son when he retired.
*Master Uril is one of the five non-[[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies to have the Curse ability, the others being the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]], [[Malevolent Dark Cat]], [[Cafeteria Cat (Enemy)|Cafeteria Cat]] and [[Sage of Selection Darvin]].

